## Failure diagnosis and remaining scope

The earlier test fixture's nonblocking listener left accepted sockets nonblocking on Windows. Its echo worker treated a transient WouldBlock/timeout as fatal. At 50 connections the core reached the upstream, but the fixture received only the preflight payload. Accepted sockets are now explicitly made blocking, transient idle timeouts are retried until shutdown, and both 50- and 2,000-connection runs pass. The test also seeds StatsService with zero counters before traffic and asserts that observed session totals equal the core totals.

The test now uses a probed port range beginning at 21808, an explicit loopback bind and MATCH,DIRECT route, and a temporary Mihomo data directory. The earlier 11808-range attempt's separate contribution was not isolated. This evidence does not satisfy SP-22's full 10k-node/10k-connection long-stability requirement, UI/FRB user-flow acceptance, or 24-hour resource-growth check; SP-22 remains implemented, not verified.
